' 4+1 process view - Refresh in the browser · Web Lock between tabs and silent refresh on /login
' Version 1.1 - 2026-11-10
' For: whoever writes code and whoever debugs.
' Documented decision: Only one tab renews the session at a time (Web Lock) and the server never renews it (ADR 0002).
' Not drawn: internal detail of the classes; refusals that do not change the sequence (they are in the text of process.md).
@startuml process-refresh-client
!include ../style.puml

title Process view - refresh in the browser: Web Lock between tabs and silent refresh on /login
autonumber

participant "tab A" as WEB_API_CLIENT
participant "tab B" as WEB_API_CLIENT_B
participant "Browser" as C_BROWSER
participant "API" as C_API
participant "Login page" as WEB_F_AUTH

== Two tabs get 401 at the same time (expired access token) ==
WEB_API_CLIENT -> C_API : GET /api/… → 401
WEB_API_CLIENT_B -> C_API : GET /api/… → 401
WEB_API_CLIENT -> C_BROWSER : locks.request('sportsbooking-refresh')
WEB_API_CLIENT_B -> C_BROWSER : locks.request('sportsbooking-refresh'): waits
C_BROWSER --> WEB_API_CLIENT : Lock granted to A
WEB_API_CLIENT -> C_API : Repeats the original request first → 401 again
WEB_API_CLIENT -> C_API : refreshSession(): POST /api/auth/refresh (only one per tab,\nrefreshInFlight)
C_API --> WEB_API_CLIENT : 204 + Set-Cookie (new cookies, shared by the tabs)
WEB_API_CLIENT -> C_API : Repeats the request → 200
WEB_API_CLIENT -> C_BROWSER : Releases the lock
C_BROWSER --> WEB_API_CLIENT_B : Lock granted to B
WEB_API_CLIENT_B -> C_API : Repeats the original request first → 200 with the cookies A\nrenewed: does not refresh
note over WEB_API_CLIENT, C_API: Without the lock, A and B would present the same refresh token; the second would be\nreuse\nand the API would revoke all sessions. Without navigator.locks: only sharing within the\ntab.\nIf the refresh fails, the 401 reaches the caller (who sends the user to /login).

== Silent refresh on /login (the server never renews the session) ==
WEB_F_AUTH -> WEB_F_AUTH : useQuery(['auth','silent-session'])
WEB_F_AUTH -> C_BROWSER : trySilentRefresh(): locks.request('sportsbooking-refresh',\nrefreshSession)
WEB_F_AUTH -> C_API : POST /api/auth/refresh
alt 204
  WEB_F_AUTH -> C_API : fetchCurrentUser(): GET /api/auth/me → account
  WEB_F_AUTH -> WEB_F_AUTH : setQueryData(['auth','me']); router.replace(safeNext(next,\nprofile))
else 401
  WEB_F_AUTH -> WEB_F_AUTH : Shows the LoginForm
end
@enduml
